-- ModalityInfer admits `main` as PNormal: `helper` ignores its argument,
-- because the inner lambda drops h1. The IR compiler's Bottom-argument Apply
-- arm refuses, on the grounds that the callee "reads its value": it sees h0
-- occur in the redex `(\h1 -> Normal) h0` and does not reduce it first.
-- Idealized: p(0.0) is the standard normal density, dim 1. The twin with a
-- constant body, `(\h1 -> 1.0) h0`, compiles since its law is a known point
-- (higher-order/admittedCalleeIgnoresBottomArgument, task
-- dispatch-on-law-certificates); this one keeps the ticket's mechanism.
-- Verified on dev at compiler 6563026. Ticket
-- admitted-callee-ignores-bottom-argument.
expect-failure: refused "the argument has pType Bottom"
